      "message": "In the current situation, it might not be possible to achieve this.\n\nAfter experimentation, setting `Android.bp` as follows:\n```\nprebuilt_root {\n    name: \"ramdisk_node_list\",\n    src: \"ramdisk_node_list\",\n    product_specific: true,\n} \n```\nresults in the final installation location being:\n`./out/target/product/vsoc_x86_64/product/ramdisk_node_list`\nHowever, we need it to be installed at:\n`./out/target/product/vsoc_x86_64/ramdisk_node_list`\n\nThe reason for the extra `product` subdirectory is that `ProductPath()` still has a default value of product even when no product variables are specified in the product configuration.\n```\n\t\t} else if ctx.ProductSpecific() || ctx.InstallInProduct() {\n\t\t\tpartition \u003d ctx.DeviceConfig().ProductPath()\n```\n```\nfunc (c *deviceConfig) ProductPath() string {\n    if c.config.productVariables.ProductPath !\u003d nil {\n        return *c.config.productVariables.ProductPath\n    }\n    return \"product\"   \n\n}\n```",
